{"step_index":100,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T17:52:33Z","content":"Report is ready. Here's the answer to your key question:\n\n### @FactTechz — Long-Form vs Shorts Revenue\n\n| Format | Monthly Views | Monthly Revenue | % of Revenue |\n|--------|-------------|----------------|-------------|\n| **Long-form** | 94.7M | **\\$408,009** | **99.1%** |\n| **Shorts** | 92.4M | **\\$3,702** | **0.9%** |\n| **Total** | 187.1M | **\\$411,711** | 100% |\n\n**The brutal reality**: Both formats get almost identical views (~94M each), but long-form earns **110x more**. Shorts RPM is \\$0.04 vs long-form RPM of \\$4.31.\n\n### Last 3 Months & Lifetime\n\n| Period | Earnings |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Last 3 months** | **~\\$1.24 Million** |\n| **Per year (current rate)** | **~\\$4.94 Million/year** |\n| **Lifetime (~10 years)** | **~\\$25-33 Million** |\n\n### The Secret\n\nDespite being an **India-based Hindi channel**, 77.8% of traffic comes from NRIs in US/UK/CA/AU → RPM of \\$4.31 instead of the typical \\$0.50-1.00 for Indian channels. This geographic arbitrage is why FactTechz earns \\$411K/month."}
